     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this one as written, even with your confirmation. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is a toxic dose, and I know of no indication or guideline that supports it. In a 70 kg adult it risks profound vasodilatory shock, and its long half-life of 30\u201350 hours would let the drug accumulate over repeated daily doses. I'm not comfortable placing an order I expect to seriously harm the patient, and a note on the order wouldn't change that risk.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum labeled dose. If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, I can also enter a second agent from a different class, such as an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide, if you tell me which one.\n- **Hold the order** while you discuss it with pharmacy. If you have an unusual rationale, pharmacy can review it and help you through your hospital's process for a non-standard dose.\n\nTell me which you'd like, or give me a different dose to enter."
      }
     ],
